  Interpretation:
    Small r is the finite gap-side avatar of a near-1/14 optimum.  In this
    bounded S3 census, the same rows still have positive CRT witness density;
    the obstruction is therefore not a single pair denominator by itself, but
    a covering-system alignment that would have to erase every rho_q witness.

========================================================================================
TAKEAWAY
========================================================================================
  The density formulation gives an interval-residue reservoir: rho*(P,E)>0
  turns into linearly many grid opportunities; the actual CRT witnesses are
  the aligned subset where the finite fast phase also lands correctly.
  The small-r denominator language is equivalent only after all other runners
  clear at the same crossing.  The useful next lemma should therefore bound
  the ability of the conditional blockers to cover the rho* reservoir, rather
  than trying to prove a private pair-denominator inequality in isolation.
